# #5851 widened catch-up (a5e2e2ef, #5851 comment 6668868649): the catch-up is a true replay
# to max(reported bound, close head - 1) on the tick. C's Replay, which reads one durable entry at
# a time to any target, is every such catch-up; these mutations break W1-W3.
MODULE: SiblingHintHonestCatchUpPassesCarriedStaleHigh
TARGET: SiblingHintHonest
CLASS: Invariant
PERTURBS: SplitHeads
SUMMARY: the split's cut does not re-read the carried close's stale high in its own turn but reuses the value a catch-up read earlier (W2), so a stale donor write landing after that catch-up is below the hint and never handed to the sibling
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithSplitHint = TRUE, WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 0, WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ seenU' = [seenU EXCEPT ![a] = Max2(@, ReportU)]
    /\ ReportStale(a)
    /\ UNCHANGED <<walVars, leafVars, epochVars, handVars, envVars, moveVars>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the cut reuses an earlier read of the stale high.
    /\ seenU' = [seenU EXCEPT ![a] = Max2(@, ReportU)]
    /\ UNCHANGED seenS
    /\ UNCHANGED <<walVars, leafVars, epochVars, handVars, envVars, moveVars>>
--- END
